<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24372" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter-nōdĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n.
		nodus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the space between two knots</i> or <i>joints</i>, <i>an internode</i> or <i>joint.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of plants: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">harundinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 2, 2, § 21</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of
			the leg: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mollia nervosus facit internodia poples,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					6, 256</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the leg</i>
			itself: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">longa internodia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Calp.
					Ecl. 1, 26</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
